# live-political-analysis — Cline instructions

This repo's full conventions live in `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/agents/*.md`. Read
those directly when working here — this file is a condensed, Cline-specific
adaptation, not a replacement.

## Scope: what Cline is for here

This repo uses a split workflow (decided 2026-08-17): judgment-heavy work —
scoping, design/visual decisions, editorial calls on sensitive content,
anything hard to reverse — happens in a separate planning session (Claude
Code), which produces a fully-specified GitHub issue. **Cline's job is to
execute an already-specified task, not to make the judgment calls itself.**

**If a task you're given isn't fully specified** — it asks you to make a
design/visual choice, a call on sensitive editorial content, or a decision
that would be expensive to undo — **stop and say so instead of guessing.**
Report back what's undecided rather than picking an answer. This is the
substitute for the model-escalation this repo would otherwise do (see
`docs/agents/model-effort.md`) — you're running on DeepSeek, not Claude, so
route judgment calls back to the human instead of resolving them yourself.

## Issue tracker

Issues live as GitHub issues on `IlhamKassim/live-political-analysis`, via
the `gh` CLI (see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`):

- Read a ticket: `gh issue view <number> --comments`
- Comment: `gh issue comment <number> --body "..."`
- Labels: `gh issue edit <number> --add-label "..."` / `--remove-label "..."`
- Label vocabulary (`docs/agents/triage-labels.md`): `needs-triage`,
  `needs-info`, `ready-for-agent`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix`.
- PRs are not a request surface — issues only.

## Domain vocabulary

`CONTEXT.md` at the repo root is the glossary — canonical terms (Coalition,
Seat, Majority, Projection, Seat Call, Audience, Return Trigger, etc.) and
words to avoid. Use its terms exactly; don't introduce synonyms. If a task
needs a new term or seems to conflict with an existing one, flag it rather
than deciding silently — term definitions are a judgment call per the rule
above.

`docs/adr/` holds architecture decisions — in particular:
- ADR 0002/0006: zero recurring cost, static site, no persistent server.
- ADR 0003/0005: never say "prediction"/"forecast" — use "Projection"/"Seat
  Call"; every Seat Call is framed as arithmetic against the GE15 Baseline,
  never as a bespoke judgement about that seat.

## Guardrails (Cline has no sandboxing here — these are load-bearing)

- **Never run `git push`, open a PR, or merge anything.** Local commits only,
  and only when explicitly asked. Report the diff; let the human decide.
- **Never run destructive git** (`reset --hard`, `clean -f`, `checkout --`,
  force-push, branch deletion) without being explicitly told to.
- **Never add a recurring-cost dependency or external API call** without
  flagging it first — this project has a hard zero-cost constraint (ADR
  0002/0006).
- Stay inside this repo's working tree. Don't touch files elsewhere on the
  machine.
- Run the existing test suite before reporting a task done; don't claim
  success from your own narrative if the tests weren't actually run.
